# Build context filter, shared by both images (each is built from the repo
# root so the web image can copy deploy/security-headers.conf, which is the
# single source of truth for the response headers).
#
# Keep this tight: everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon on
# every build, and backend/.venv plus frontend/node_modules are together
# larger than the images themselves.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Secrets
#
# Real configuration is passed as environment variables at run time and must
# never be baked into a layer. `.env.example` is deliberately still included:
# it is the tracked template and contains no secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Python
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- Node
**/node_modules
**/.vite
# Stale incremental state from a host `tsc -b` would make the in-image build
# skip emit and produce nothing.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# -------------------------------------------------------------- Build output
# The image builds its own; a host dist/ would silently win the COPY.
frontend/dist

# ------------------------------------------------------------- Runtime data
**/.data
backend/.data-*

# --------------------------------------------------- Tests, docs, scratch
backend/tests
e2e
docs
README.md
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright
**/*.log
